# =====================================================================
# .dockerignore for the AircraftSaaS solution (used by every .WebHost
# Dockerfile under Services/*/Dockerfile, build context = AircraftSaaS/).
#
# Goal: keep the build context tight and prevent secrets / dev artefacts
# from ever entering an image layer. Anything matched here is invisible
# to `docker build`, including the build stage's `COPY . .`.
# =====================================================================

# --- Source control & IDE noise ----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitlab-ci.yml
.github
.vs
.vscode
.idea
*.user
*.suo
*.DS_Store

# --- Build outputs (must be rebuilt inside the build stage) ------------
**/bin
**/obj
**/bin/Debug
**/bin/Release
**/obj/Debug
**/obj/Release
bin/
obj/
dist/
out/
publish/
**/TestResults

# --- Node / frontend artefacts (not in this context but defensive) -----
node_modules/

# --- Test projects (we don't run tests inside the runtime image build) -
**/*Tests/**
**/*.Tests/**
**/*Test.csproj
**/*Tests.csproj

# --- Compose / local dev configs we never want baked into images -------
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# --- Secrets & local environment files ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
secrets.json

# --- Misc ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
README.md
README_LOCAL.md
*.md
